Final verification report: Phase 3 - Kafka consumer (the actual US-5.2 behavior)

Automated tests: sbt scalafmtCheck test -> 95/95 passed, formatting clean (includes StockEventConsumerSuite's 4 real-Kafka Testcontainers tests covering success, failure, unknown-item no-op, and already-resolved-order no-op).

Manual verification: added a Kafka service to docker-compose.yml (local dev needs it now that the service runs a real consumer on startup - previously missing). Ran scripts/verify-stock-event-consumer.sh - real order-service instance, real Postgres, real Kafka (docker-compose, not Testcontainers), two checkouts reset to pending via direct SQL (isolating the consumer from the synchronous reserve outcome, which is unrelated to this phase), then published real inventory.stock-reserved/-reservation-failed messages via the broker's own console producer. Confirmed both orders' status flipped correctly (reserved / reservation_failed) through the live background consumer wired into Main.scala.

Debugging note: the first two script attempts hit a NullPointerException ('bytes is null') inside fs2-kafka's String key deserializer - root-caused (with web research) to kafka-console-producer.sh sending a NULL key by default, which fs2-kafka's Deserializer.string doesn't handle gracefully (a known class of gap in fs2-kafka's convenience deserializers, see fd4s/fs2-kafka#992 for the same pattern in their Avro deserializer). Not a broker-version or order-service code issue - fixed by having the script's publish() set an explicit key (--property parse.key=true), matching the pattern StockEventConsumerSuite's own producer helper already used. All checks passed after the fix.
